id: 28
hanzi: 支
pinyin: zhī
level: HSK 5
part_of_speech: Measure Word

meanings_summary:
  en: measure word for long thin inflexible objects (arrows, pens, guns), songs, or military units; to support; branch
  es: clasificador para objetos largos y rígidos (flechas, plumas, fusiles), canciones o tropas; sostener; rama

senses[2]{sense_number,part_of_speech,register,definition_en,definition_es,example_phrase}:
  1 | Measure Word | Standard | used to count slender, rigid, rod-like items such as arrows, pens, firearms, cigarettes, or candles | clasificador para objetos delgados y rígidos como flechas, bolígrafos, fusiles o velas | 一支箭 (an arrow)
  2 | Measure Word | Standard | used to count musical melodies, songs, or organized military troop units | clasificador para composiciones musicales, canciones o contingentes militares | 一支军队 (an army)

example_sentences[2]{id,hanzi,pinyin,en,es}:
  #1 | 李广将军面不改色，沉着地从身后的箭袋中抽出一支白羽长箭，搭在弓弦上瞄准猛虎。 | Lǐ Guǎng jiāngjūn miànbùgǎisè, chénzhuó de cóng shēnhòu de jiàndài zhōng chōuchū yì zhī báiyǔ chángjiàn, dā zài gōngxián shàng miáozhǔn měnghǔ. | Without turning pale, General Li Guang calmly pulled a white-feathered long arrow from his quiver, nocked it, and aimed at the tiger. | Sereno y sin mudar el semblante, el general Li Guang extrajo del carcaj una flecha de plumas blancas, la colocó en la cuerda y apuntó a la fiera.
  #2 | 音乐会上，小提琴演奏家深情地拉响了一支悠扬动听的古典名曲，引得台下观众如痴如醉。 | Yīnyuèhuì shàng, xiǎotíqín yǎnzòujiā shēnqíng de lāxiǎng le yì zhī yōuyáng dòngtīng de gǔdiǎn míngqǔ, yǐndé táixià guānzhòng rúchī-rúzuì. | At the concert, the violinist passionately performed a melodious classical piece, entrancing the audience below. | En el concierto, el virtuoso del violín interpretó con honda emoción una melodía clásica tan melodiosa que cautivó al auditorio.

collocations[6]{hanzi,en}:
  一支箭 | an arrow
  一支笔 | a pen or brush
  一支军队 | an army unit or detachment
  一支乐曲 | a piece of music; a song
  一支枪 | a rifle or gun
  支吾其词 | speak evasively; hem and haw

idioms[4]{hanzi,pinyin,meaning_en}:
  独木难支 | dú mù nán zhī | a single log cannot prop up a falling roof; cannot manage alone
  乐不可支 | lè bù kě zhī | overjoyed beyond control; overwhelmed with joy
  支离破碎 | zhī lí pò suì | broken into pieces; fragmented and disrupted
  强弩之末 | qiáng nǔ zhī mò | the dying momentum of an arrow shot from a strong crossbow

character_decomposition[1]{character,pinyin,meaning_en,meaning_es,radical,radical_meaning_en,meaning_component,sound_component,stroke_count,composition_type,etymology_and_mnemonic,visual_mnemonic_story_en,visual_mnemonic_story_es,tone_mnemonic_anchor,cangjie,traditional}:
  支 | zhī | branch; support; measure word | rama; sostener; clasificador | 支 | branch / hand holding | 又 (yòu, right hand holding branch) | 十 (bamboo bamboo shoot / branch) | 4 | 单一结构 | Ancient bronze pictogram of a right hand 又 holding a slender snapped bamboo branch 十, signifying support or counting items. | A firm hand (又) grasps a slender bamboo twig (十) to prop up a tent and count long rods (支). | Una mano diestra (又) sostiene una varilla delgada de bambú (十) para apuntalar y contar objetos finos (支). | 55 | JE | 

mnemonics_and_roots:
  composite_memory_hook_en: A hand gripping a slender bamboo branch (支) props up structures and counts arrows and pens as a measure word (支).
  composite_memory_hook_es: Una mano que empuña una varilla de bambú (支) apuntala estructuras y cuenta flechas y plumas como clasificador (支).
  cultural_and_cognitive_roots: In ancient archery and tallying, bamboo arrows and divination reeds (筹策) were counted in bundles held in hand (支). Consequently, 支 evolved from 'hand grasping branch' into both a verb of support (支撑) and the specialized classifier for stiff slender implements and melodies.
  tone_sandhi_and_pitch_modulation: High level 1st tone 'zhī' (55). Maintain a sustained, clean, ringing high pitch contour.

